The Business Case: Standardizing Real Estate Acquisition
The Client
You have been hired as a freelance data analyst by a boutique real estate investment firm, let's call them Vanguard Property Group. They specialize in purchasing single-family homes to hold as long-term rental properties.

The Pain Point
Currently, Vanguard's acquisition managers are evaluating potential properties using "back of the napkin" math and disjointed, static spreadsheets. Because they lack a standardized tool, they are struggling to objectively compare properties across different ZIP codes. Recently, they acquired a property that looked great on paper, but they failed to account for historical market stagnation in that specific neighborhood, resulting in lower-than-expected returns.

The Objective (Your Mission)
Vanguard needs a dynamic, data-driven tool to standardize their property vetting process. They need a single Excel dashboard where an acquisition manager can:

Input a property's financial variables (price, down payment, interest).

Instantly see the projected 10-year ROI and monthly cash flow.

Cross-reference those projections against historical neighborhood trends using Zillow's ZHVI and ZORI datasets.

Stress-test the investment using best-case and worst-case market scenarios.